# Pairs with RevertNeverServesRestored. The revert that leaves the restored
# copy serving: it moves the alias back and clears the previous copy's
# redirect, but never arms the shadow to forward, so a routing activation that
# cached the restored alias keeps serving - and writing - the restored copy.
MODULE: RevertNeverServesRestoredNoRedirect
TARGET: RevertNeverServesRestored
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: the revert arms no redirect on the restored copy
PERTURBS: RevertRedirect

--- FIND
    /\ redir' = [redir EXCEPT !["prev"] = "none", !["shadow"] = "prev"]
--- REPLACE
    \* MUTATION: the shadow is not armed.
    /\ redir' = [redir EXCEPT !["prev"] = "none"]
--- END
